Project 4: Loan Approval Predictor with API

What it is. A machine learning model that predicts whether a loan application is likely to be approved,
based on income, credit history, loan amount and similar fields. The trained model is served through a
FastAPI endpoint, and a small Streamlit page lets anyone enter details and see the prediction.
Why it impresses. Plenty of students train models in notebooks. Very few can put a model behind an
API with input validation and deploy it. This project joins your data skills with your backend skills,
which is exactly the profile AI focused startups look for.

Tech stack

Part                                   Use
Data                                   A public loan prediction dataset from Kaggle
ML                                     Pandas and Scikit Learn (logistic regression, random forest)
Model saving                           joblib
API                                    FastAPI with Pydantic input validation
Interface                              Streamlit calling your API
Tracking                               Store every prediction request in a database table for later review

Must have features
• A notebook with exploration, cleaning, feature engineering, and comparison of at least two models.
• Clear evaluation: confusion matrix, precision, recall, F1, and an explanation of which metric matters
most here and why.
• A /predict endpoint that validates input and returns the prediction with a probability.
• A /health endpoint and a /model_info endpoint showing model version and training date.
• A Streamlit form that calls the API.
Extra features once the basics work
• Explain each prediction using feature importance.
• Log every request and response for monitoring.
• A retraining script that saves a new model version.

