How to build it, step by step
1 Explore the data and note class imbalance, missing values and important features.
2 Train a simple baseline first, then a better model. Record the scores of both in a table.
3 Move the training code from the notebook into train.py so it can be run again cleanly.
4 Build the FastAPI service that loads the saved model once at startup and serves predictions.
5 Add strict Pydantic validation so wrong input types return a clean error.
6 Build the Streamlit form, write tests for the API, deploy, and document.
Deployment
Deploy the API on Render or Railway and the Streamlit interface on Streamlit Community Cloud,
pointing it to your API URL.
Questions this project prepares you for
• Why did you choose this model over the others?
